1
00:00:00,297 --> 00:00:02,717
(Sheldon:)Why are we all here?

2
00:00:02,883 --> 00:00:04,553
Because we're scientists.

3
00:00:05,136 --> 00:00:07,636
(Sheldon:)And what do scientists study?

4
00:00:07,805 --> 00:00:09,385
(Sheldon:)The universe.

5
00:00:09,557 --> 00:00:11,387
(Sheldon:)And what's the universe made of?

6
00:00:11,559 --> 00:00:13,809
(Sheldon:)I am so glad you asked.

7
00:00:13,978 --> 00:00:18,148
[SINGING] There's antimony, arsenic
Aluminum, selenium

8
00:00:18,315 --> 00:00:20,405
(Sheldon:)Hydrogen and oxygen
And nitrogen and rhenium

9
00:00:20,568 --> 00:00:22,858
(Sheldon:)And nickel, neodymium
Neptunium, germanium

10
00:00:23,028 --> 00:00:24,068
Everybody!

11
00:00:24,238 --> 00:00:27,078
And iron, americium
Ruthenium, uranium

12
00:00:27,241 --> 00:00:30,241
Europium, zirconium
Lutetium, vanadium

13
00:00:30,411 --> 00:00:31,491
Just the Asians!

14
00:00:31,662 --> 00:00:35,042
And lanthanum and osmium
And astatine and radium

15
00:00:51,390 --> 00:00:53,390
(Sheldon:)Penny, Leonard.

16
00:00:53,851 --> 00:00:56,521
(Sheldon:)Would you be able to answer
some questions I'm having...

17
00:00:56,687 --> 00:00:59,277
(Sheldon:)...about the events of last night?

18
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:03,020
(Sheldon:)-Sure.
-Question one.

